## Summaries

- **001** Integer interpolation model reproduces the known n=6, degree-3 fully sensitive function (control only; not a challenge result).
- **002** CP-SAT searches restricted to functions invariant under given permutation groups. Covers only the stated families.
- **003** Enumerates the 247 n=14, d=5 layer profiles (agrees with Stepanovs 2012) and orbit subset-sum filters for symmetric families.
- **004** Independent Fourier arithmetic on the 247 profiles (29 survive integral energy, 12 survive parity bounds); block-aggregate necessary conditions.
- **005** Integer-coefficient zeta-transform model with Parseval; controls pass; n=14 runs bounded and UNKNOWN (inconclusive).
- **006** Complete sparse spectral formulation, the pinned CaDiCaL/lrat-trim toolchain, sphere catalogs (orders 7 to 12) and audited exclusions (two-negative-cubic, private-vertex argument). Many files are premises of the checkpoint chain.
- **007** Bounded literature audit (2026-10-13): no source decides (n,d)=(14,5); corrects novelty claims (Stepanovs 2012 has the degree-5 bound and the 247 profiles).
- **008** Defect-budget arithmetic and exclusions of zero-pair cases; derivative catalogs used as premises of later checkpoints.
- **009** The main Codex packet (about 47k files): magnitude-pattern ledger, signed-star contexts, root-7 LRAT proofs, every checkpoint manifest, acceptance and snapshot. H in all handoffs. Navigate by pinned paths only. Tests: Only the two controls named in CLAUDE.md are in the suite; the many other cycle tests are run by their own cycle records.
- **010** Restricted construction family (NAE3 blocks plus weight-one coordinates). Solver results without independent UNSAT certificates are provisional; affects no unrestricted branch.
- **011** Level-1 + triple + Parseval SDP established no new n=14 exclusion; full-SDP feasibility is numerical only and no exact Farkas certificate was found. Negative result for this method.
- **012** 221 verified witnesses (4 at n=12, 217 at n=13), a few exact nonexistence certificates for restricted families, structural observations. Source of the 018 positive controls. Tests: verify.py is not -O safe (its checks are assert statements); its -O run is declared skipped. 012 is closed and none of it is accepted.
- **013** Dated literature search (2026-10-21): no resolution of the problem and no directly applicable SDP or flag-algebra prior art found (a negative search result, not a novelty claim); Schrijver block formula verified.
- **014** All signed-star native contexts excluded by CP-SAT cores turned into LRAT proofs (decision-diagram CNF encoder, independent verifier); root-7 c2 also on raw rows (1533). The CNF encoder is reused by 017 and 018.
- **015** Independent enumeration of triangulated 2-spheres through order 12, reproducing the 006 catalogs (orders 7 to 12) and the signed-star root domain; review of the 1412 theorem and the 1425/1431 rows, keeping 1409's inherited premises. A premise of 016 to 018.
- **016** Types I and III excluded; Type II reduced to 24 open shapes (136 classes, typed frontier with independent reader).
- **017** The 24 shapes fall to 3184 LRAT case certificates checked by an independent reader, over an exact cover checked against every labelled placement. Closes the one-free residual-six case (conditional on its AI-reviewed lemmas). certs/ is about 13 GB.
- **018** Frontier of the 22 open patterns with remaining defect <= 6 (union 14 forced). Lemma L1 with a 2221-case cover; certificate run (4442 obligations) in progress. Nothing accepted.

## Status legend

- `accepted`: results accepted into the listed checkpoints.
- `foundational`: Codex-era packet whose accepted files are premises pinned by the current checkpoint.
- `in_progress`: active; nothing accepted.
- `closed`: finished without an accepted result (exploratory, negative or a report).
- `historical`: early Codex-era packet, kept for reference.
# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Status: problem OPEN; Claude Code orchestrates, Codex consults

Codex paused research on 2026-10-21. Claude Code resumed it on the user's
request: attempts 011 to 018, and checkpoints 1531 to 1533 on 2026-10-23.
Since 2026-10-23 Claude Code orchestrates (the user's choice). It consults
Codex through `.research/tools/consult_codex.py` (read-only, recorded under
`<attempt>/consultations/`) for independent review, critique and ideas.
Codex's answers are AI review, never acceptance. Curate what is used into
`REVIEW-*-codex.md`.
**Do not start a search, solver run or experiment just because this
directory was opened.** Read these first; they outrank this file:
- `.research/CODEX_BRIEFING.md`: current frontier, the in-flight 018 run,
  open issues and conventions. It is also the context given to Codex when
  it is consulted.
- `.research/attempts/INDEX.md`: every attempt, generated from its
  `ATTEMPT.json`.
- `.research/state.md`: the latest checkpoint summary, via
  `current-checkpoint.json`.
- `.research/CLAUDE_HANDOFF.md`: history and corrections up to 1530.

## Two projects share this tree

1. **Active: Boolean degree vs. sensitivity** (`.research/`, ~120 GB, ~55k
   files). Question: does a Boolean multilinear f on 14 variables exist with
   real degree ≤ 5, f(0)=0 and f(e_i)=1 for all i? This is the d=5 case of
   Epoch AI's "sensitivity vs. degree" challenge (`.research/goal.md`): beat
   sensitivity d^(log 6/log 3) ≈ 13.8 at d=5, so full sensitivity 14 at the
   origin. The authoritative statement is `.research/active-objective.md`.
   Done means one of two things: (a) a construction checked independently
   on all 16,384 inputs, including exact degree, or (b) a nonexistence proof
   covering every case, with checkable certificates. Pruning, a necessary
   profile, a ternary derivative, a prefix, a local obstruction or a solver
   UNKNOWN is not completion.
2. **Dormant: no-three-in-line** (`src/math_theory/`, `tests/`, `docs/`,
   `experiments/`). This is the only conventional Python package here and
   the project `README.md` describes. n=71 is open; every bounded run was
   UNKNOWN (`docs/experiment-log.md`, `docs/sat-attack.md`).

## Commands

```sh
